<newsitem itemid="78508" id="root" date="1996-09-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: Pacific Century returns to black.</title>
<headline>Pacific Century returns to black.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss	  (gain)   0.84   vs   6.34   (loss)</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	(gain)   0.54   vs   4.12   (loss)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     51.95   vs  51.71</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest    45.18   vs  35.78</p>
<p>    Interest expense		    1.56   vs   0.48</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  3.51   vs   2.80</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    (gain)   0.49   vs   6.50   (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.11   vs   0.07</p>
<p>    Minorities		 (loss)   0.76   vs   0.23   (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  (loss)   0.64   vs   0.08   (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Pacific Century Regional Developments Ltd attributed the improvement in results to a positive contribution from its insurance subsidiary and the start of operations of its China power plant.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
